Fixed. The issue was an orphaned `);` left over from removing the `message_tags` and `drop_queue` CREATE TABLE statements. The SQL became:

```sql
    );        ← closes session_stats (correct)
    );        ← ORPHAN — was the closing of drop_queue before deletion
```

And an empty `if` block in the migration:

```typescript
if (!statsCols.includes("total_auto_prunes")) {
}
```

Both fixed now. Schema has 5 clean CREATE TABLE statements (`compression_blocks`, `tool_calls`, `session_stats`, `facts`, `raw_transcripts`) — no more dangling syntax. Should init cleanly on `/reload`.
